          "message": {
            "text": "The isolation boundary deliberately begins before background-color. Blink's BoxPainterBase::PaintFillLayers opens one separate buffer around reverse FillLayer painting, and its bottom FillLayer owns both the color and image; grouping only SVG image rects therefore changes the backdrop for the bottom blend.",
            "markdown": "The isolation boundary deliberately begins before background-color. Blink's BoxPainterBase::PaintFillLayers opens one separate buffer around reverse FillLayer painting, and its bottom FillLayer owns both the color and image; grouping only SVG image rects therefore changes the backdrop for the bottom blend."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/element-tree-to-svg.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 4488,
                  "endLine": 4502,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    const backgroundImageStart = svgParts.length;\n    state.bgClipTextFills.set(el, paintBackgroundImageLayers(paintCtx, el, indent, corners, useInlineFragments, captureViewport));\n    const blendLayers = splitTopLevelCommas(el.styles.backgroundBlendMode ?? \"normal\");\n    const hasNonNormalBlend = blendLayers.some((mode) => mode.trim() !== \"\" && mode.trim() !== \"normal\");\n    // Blink's BoxPainterBase opens its separate buffer around PaintFillLayers,\n    // whose bottom FillLayer paints both the background color and its image.\n    // Keep the same boundary here: isolating only image rects leaves the\n    // bottom blended layer with a transparent backdrop instead of the color.\n    if (hasNonNormalBlend && svgParts.length > backgroundImageStart) {\n      const stack = svgParts.slice(backgroundStackStart).join(\"\\n\");\n      svgParts.length = backgroundStackStart;\n      svgParts.push(`${indent}<g style=\"isolation:isolate\">\\n${stack}\\n${indent}</g>`);\n    }\n  }\n  const { fills: textBgClipFills, fragmentFills: textBgClipFragmentFills } = state.bgClipTextFills.get(el) ?? { fills: [], fragmentFills: [] };"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
